  "slug": "perturbation-profiling-e9d8",
  "summary": "Spatial, small-molecule and barcode-based chromatin profiling now links perturbations to accessibility, hub organization and enhancer rewiring.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is resolving how regulatory state responds to perturbation or cell-state change, using chromatin-level readouts. Perturb-Tags pairs spatially barcoded CRISPR perturbations with single-nucleus expression and chromatin accessibility, revealing non-autonomous transcriptomic and epigenomic responses. MolMap extends this to unmodified small molecules, profiling genome-wide accessibility changes in non-crosslinked nuclei and reporting early, compound-specific responses. On the mechanistic side, live imaging shows that hindsight transcription in response to Notch is sustained by a handover from Mastermind to Broad transcription hubs over time, while Hi-C and HiChIP across three differentiation systems show super-enhancers rewiring extensively. AMBER adds a mapping approach, linking accessible chromatin through hydrogel-assisted barcode seed expansion to multi-scale regulatory hubs in mouse brain cells. The new element is the combination of perturbation-resolved, spatially and temporally explicit chromatin readouts.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
